  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Imported from the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, which cities file themselves and which runs through 2025. Not yet checked against the city's own project list.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001099",
        "SRC-001107"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC CA-25-590: Gateway Tower, located at 470 South Market Street in San Jose on a 0.5 acre site, requested and is being recommended for a reservation of $9,524,617 in annual federal tax credits and $12,695,387 in total state tax credits and $95,423,012 of tax-exempt bond cap to finance the new construction of 220 units of housing, consisting of 218 restricted rental units and 2 unrestricted manager's units.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001663"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the October 2026 closing, J.P. Morgan stated over $123.4 million in construction financing and over $93.6 million in federal and state tax credit equity through Enterprise Community Investment, Inc. The August 2025 state report's plan shows $129.5 million in construction loans and $95.6 million in equity, so the financing table above reflects the earlier plan.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001917",
        "SRC-001663"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Core's president credits the City of San Jose, County of Santa Clara, Santa Clara Housing Authority, CalHFA, Housing Trust of Silicon Valley, Enterprise and JPMorgan Chase.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001917"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "San Jose Spotlight reported a $38 million city loan, approved in late September 2025, and a $64 million county loan. The August 2025 state report shows $45.83 million from the county and no separate city line.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001920",
        "SRC-001663"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Set-asides as reported: 55 units for the county's rapid rehousing program; about 10 for SoFA artists; 65 project-based vouchers. DLR Group's page describes 120 supportive units, half for formerly unhoused people.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001917",
        "SRC-001920",
        "SRC-001919",
        "SRC-001921"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "221,000 square feet, designed for LEED Silver.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001921"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "San Jose Jazz is expected to be a ground-floor commercial tenant. The historic Herrold College facade is kept, with an exhibit on Charles 'Doc' Herrold and the birth of radio broadcasting.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001918",
        "SRC-001917",
        "SRC-001920"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Parcels: 264-30-090 came from state data. 264-30-114 was added by matching 493 S 1st St, the address San Jose Spotlight gives, to the county parcel. Spotlight describes three buildings between 493 S First St and 480 S Market St, and other parcels on the site may not be listed here yet.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001920",
        "SRC-001098"
      ]
    }
  ],
